Z||000000||gearhead313||04-17-2001||02:19 PM||||I have my 85 gt here, and there is so much wheel gap, that i could set up a 3-ring circus in it!!!...so, I NEED TO LOWER!!<P>my question is, who has the best springs out there, and of course, the best price...oh ya, i am not cutting my springs for anybody out there who has done that, i want to do it the right way,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  thanks for the help!!<P>------------------<BR>85 fiero GT 4-speed<BR>2.8 V6 .060 over<BR>big cam and head work...<BR>"~5LTRETR~"||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroLisa||04-17-2001||02:41 PM||||Do a search (link located under "post reply", there have been a ton of posts on all the different lowering options  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT- 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air,<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>Tarheels Fieros Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||danny boy||04-17-2001||04:18 PM||||The best way to lower is with drop spindles. Not the cheapest, but the best. This keeps the suspension geometry the same. Don't think they are available for the rear,So I will highly recommend coilovers.HIGHLY RECOMMEND COILOVERS. Aside from the Grant Corsa steeringwheel I had in my old coupe, These are the best things I ever put on a Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Will||04-17-2001||04:54 PM||||Budget lowering kit:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.kalecoauto.com/appear.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.kalecoauto.com/appear.htm</A> ||||reg||1
